{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared Python<->TypeScript contract for the covapp coverage report.",
    "web/src/covapp/types.ts re-declares, by hand and with no compiler in",
    "between, the shape of everything spa_data.py emits: the data-format",
    "version, every payload's keys, the closed per-line state vocabulary",
    "(vs STATE_COLORS in coverage/colors.py), the sentinel ticket ids as TS",
    "string literals, the window callback names the emitted chunk scripts",
    "invoke, and the cov_data/ directory layout data.ts fetches from. This",
    "table is the single source of truth for all of them, asserted from BOTH",
    "sides -- Python by tests/unit/cov/test_covapp_contract.py (against real",
    "emitted payloads, never a copied list) and TypeScript by",
    "web/src/covapp/contract.test.ts (against `Record<keyof X, true>`, so the",
    "compiler catches a drifting interface before the runtime check does).",
    "A drift on either side fails exactly one suite and names the divergent",
    "language. Same shape as the format_outage_cases.json precedent."
  ],
